  QUEUE_ITEM
  MANUAL
  GUARD_CASE
  /// Acted on from the content page; `sourceId` is the content's id and `sourceTargetType` says
  /// which kind, because content ids are only unique within their own type.
  CONTENT
}

/// What an internal note is about. One note table serves every subject, so the kinds live here.
enum NoteSubjectType {
  MEMBER
  SUPPORT_THREAD
  REPORT_CASE
  GUARD_CASE
  DISPUTE
  MANAGED_REQUEST
  BRIEF
  DEAL
  ESCALATION
}

/// What a staff export is of (§5.26). One row per kind the portal can ask for, even where the
/// list behind it is not built yet: the enum is the contract, and a kind that is refused at
/// request time is a clearer answer than a kind the portal cannot name.
enum AdminExportKind {
  MEMBERS
  AUDIT
  REPORTS
  ENFORCEMENT
  CONTENT
  SUPPORT_THREADS
  /// Reserved. Chart CSVs are produced in the browser from the payload the staff member already
  /// has, so no new data leaves the API (§5.26); the kind exists so the portal's audit event and
  /// this enum agree about what a chart download is called.
  ANALYTICS_CHART
}

/// Where an export has got to. `EXPIRED` is the file going away after seven days (S12.2), not the
/// row: the row is kept a year, because "who exported every member's email address in March" is a
/// question the trail has to be able to answer.
enum AdminExportState {
  QUEUED
  RUNNING
  READY
  FAILED
  EXPIRED
}

/// How risky a piece of content scored (§6.3). The tiers are the thresholds staff tune in
/// `SystemConfig`, not constants in code: a lexicon that cannot be retuned without a deploy is one
/// nobody retunes.
enum ContentRiskTier {
  CLEAN
  LOW
  MEDIUM
  HIGH
  CRITICAL
}

/// Whether the public can see a piece of content, and if not, how far it is hidden (§6.5).
///
/// Deliberately not a boolean, and deliberately not the same thing as removal: staff removal stays
/// `deletedAt`, because "removed" is a decision and these are states a scan or an approval queue
/// puts content into. The difference between LIMITED and HELD is the one members feel — a limited
/// post is still on its author's profile and reachable by link, a held one is not visible to
/// anybody but its author, who is told it is under review.
enum ContentVisibilityState {
  VISIBLE
  /// Medium tier: out of feeds, search, Pulse and recommendations; still on the author's profile
  /// and at a direct link.
  LIMITED
  /// High or critical, or a staff hide: not public at all. The author sees "under review".
  HELD
  /// An anonymous post waiting for Trust & Safety (§7.4).
  PENDING_APPROVAL
  /// Rejected — an anonymous post refused, or a held item turned down. The author sees why.
  REJECTED
}

/// How far a scan got. `DEGRADED` is the honest one: the lexicon ran and the classifier did not,
/// so the verdict stands on half the evidence and `safety.rescan-degraded` will try again (§6.7).
enum ContentScanStatus {
  PENDING
  COMPLETE
  DEGRADED
  FAILED
}

enum ContentScanTrigger {
  CREATE
  EDIT
  RESCAN
  REPORT
  MANUAL
}

/// What a reviewer's decision said about a term that matched. This is how a lexicon gets better:
/// a term whose hits are mostly `FALSE_POSITIVE` is a term that is costing staff time.
enum RiskTermHitOutcome {
  PENDING
  CONFIRMED
  FALSE_POSITIVE
}
